# Build output and dependencies are reproducible from the sources; the install
# scripts copy dist/ but never expect it to be committed.
# Written without a trailing slash on purpose: `make bootstrap` borrows
# node_modules as a *symlink* in a gate worktree, and a directory-only pattern
# does not match one — so the isolated checkout read as dirty.
node_modules
dist
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
